 "equipment_type": "Chiller",
 "applies_to": "Daikin Applied Magnitude WMC E-vintage water-cooled magnetic-bearing centrifugal chillers with the MicroTech unit controller and BACnet/Modbus communication module set to Modbus, per ED 19131-1.",
 "summary": "Water-cooled magnetic-bearing centrifugal chiller (Magnitude WMC, E vintage) on the MicroTech unit controller. A plug-in BAS module set to Modbus RTU exposes 16-bit holding registers: evaporator, condenser and heat-recovery water temperatures, refrigerant pressures and temperatures per compressor, compressor amps/volts/kW, pump status and hours, enable/mode/heat-setpoint commands, status enums and alarm index/module registers. Values follow an English/Metric setting.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 19200,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "1-based",
  "note": "ED 19131 prints holding registers without the 4xxxx prefix (register 8 = 40008) and states the module is zero-based: 40002 is sent as 0001. Wire address = printed number - 1."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "MicroTech Unit Controller Protocol Information - BACnet and Modbus Networks, Chiller Models AGZ-F, WMC-E and WMT (ED 19131-1)",
  "doc_number": "ED 19131-1",
  "revision_date": "2026-04",
  "url": "https://tahoeweb.daikinapplied.com/api/general/DownloadDocumentByName/media/ED%2019131-1.pdf/",
  "pages": "p. 4 (defaults), pp. 7-9 (addressing, word order), p. 10 (Table 5 points by model), pp. 18-24 (Tables 11-13), pp. 31-33 (Modbus alarm registers)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Network setup and parameter ranges come from the companion manual IM 1283-1, BACnet and Modbus Chiller Unit Controller (Mar 2024), pp. 36-39: https://tahoeweb.daikinapplied.com/api/general/DownloadDocumentByName/media/IM1283-1.pdf/",
  "Two-register counters: the document's worked example (99900 = 0x0001863C stored as 74 = 0x0001, 75 = 0x863C) puts the high word first, so they are ABCD.",
  "The document never defines 'x 10'. Its ranges and defaults ('Default: 100% x 10', '-40-230°F x 10') only make sense as raw = value x 10, so those registers use scale 0.1.",
  "Signedness is not stated. Temperatures and refrigerant pressures are INT16 because their published ranges go negative (the pressure rows include sub-atmospheric R-1233zd(E) ranges); counters, percentages and enums are UINT16.",
  "Units follow the HMI 'BAS Measurement Units' setting, readable at register 316 (English default). Units shown are English (°F, psi); Metric uses °C and kPa with the same multiplier.",
  "Units (316) shows 'RW Holding Register' in the data-type column but 'R' in the access column; it is listed read-only (change it at the HMI).",
  "Compressor points are listed for the Circuit 1 Compressor 1 and Compressor 2 slots that Table 12 gives for current, %RLA, power, voltage and pressures; run hours and starts use the same two slots.",
  "Left out: evaporator and condenser flow rates (18, 21). They are printed as 0-65,535 GPM / 0-4134.6 L/S with no multiplier, so the Metric scaling is not settled.",
  "Alarm index meanings (pp. 32-33) are not reproduced; the module-type value list is the same for all classes.",
  "ED 19131 is shared with AGZ-F and WMT chillers. Only points that Table 5 marks in the WMC-E column are listed.",
  "Left out: Cool Setpoint - Network (35). Table 5 marks it for WMC-E, but its range cell gives only WMT and AGZ-F ranges, so the WMC-E scaling is not printed. The setpoint in use can still be read at Active Setpoint (12).",
  "Heat Setpoint - Network (37) shows 'RO Holding Register' in the data-type column but 'R/W' access, and is described as changing the setpoint from the network; it is listed RW.",
  "Left out: points Table 5 does not mark for WMC-E (ice setpoint, outdoor air temperature)."
 ],
